    "title": "Margate Paints the Town Bright Green - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joe Kelly ,\n7 hours ago\nThe color in Margate, New Jersey is definitely green.\nRoad crews have spent the last few weeks making sure everyone notices.\nJoe Kelly\nMargate New Jersey Paints Atlantic Avenue Green\nIf you’re been on Atlantic Avenue in Margate the last few days, you’ve probably noticed that part of the street is painted green!\nIt’s the bike lane, and crews have been painting for the last couple of weeks.\nI’ll say this: it really makes that bike lane shine!\nThis is a practice that began a few years ago, and the purpose is to improve safety and really make the bike lane stand out.\nJoe Kelly\nOne thing it attempts to accomplish is it keeps drivers from using the bike lane to make right turns or to pass other vehicles.\nThis time of the year, there are some bicyclists that use the lane, but in the summer, it’s a busy place! Bike riders, cars, and pedestrians, all near the beach.\nKudos to Margate for continuing to put the emphasis on safety. The safety of bicyclists, pedestrians and drivers!\nAdd to Preferred Sources",
    "summary": "Margate New Jersey Paints Atlantic Avenue Green If you’re been on Atlantic Avenue in Margate the last few days, you’ve probably noticed that part of the street is painted green! This is a practice that began a few years ago, and the purpose is to improve safety and really make the bike lane stand out. One thing it attempts to accomplish is it keeps drivers from using the bike lane to make right turns or to pass other vehicles. This time of the year, there are some bicyclists that use the lane, but in the summer, it’s a busy place!",
